        {
            "content_html": "<img src=\"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/26078826?u=9388a2c2a0f1ca2799a4fd23f3e060c353d6ac37&v=4\" width=\"64\" height=\"64\" alt=\"\"/><br/><h3 dir=\"auto\">Description</h3>\n<p dir=\"auto\">Remove redundant indefinite articles <code class=\"notranslate\">a</code> from var/param/etc names (e.g. <code class=\"notranslate\">aCar</code> -&gt; <code class=\"notranslate\">car</code>).</p>\n<p dir=\"auto\">Mostly this is just grepping <code class=\"notranslate\">\\ba([A-Z])(\\w{2,30}(?![+/=])\\b)</code> and replacing with <code class=\"notranslate\">\\l$1$2</code>, with a few context-sensitive exceptions.</p>\n<p dir=\"auto\">Excluded cases where the <code class=\"notranslate\">a</code> had a clear purpose (e.g. <code class=\"notranslate\">aElem</code> = an anchor element), as well as files under <code class=\"notranslate\">mozilla/firefox/releases</code> (release notes) and <code class=\"notranslate\">webgl*,webxr*</code> (I don't know if webgl has some convention around this or if the <code class=\"notranslate\">a</code>s there had some significance).</p>\n<h3 dir=\"auto\">Motivation</h3>\n<p dir=\"auto\">Per linked issue</p>\n<h3 dir=\"auto\">Additional details</h3>\n<p dir=\"auto\">Bikeshedding — does MDN have a general style preference between <code class=\"notranslate\">showDefaultUI</code> vs <code class=\"notranslate\">showDefaultUi</code> style for camel-cased vars? The <a href=\"https://developer.mozilla.org/en-US/docs/MDN/Writing_guidelines/Code_style_guide/JavaScript#variable_names\" rel=\"nofollow\">writing guide</a> currently doesn't seem to mention it.</p>\n<h3 dir=\"auto\">Related issues and pull requests</h3>\n<p dir=\"auto\"><span class=\"issue-keyword tooltipped tooltipped-se\" aria-label=\"This pull request closes issue #40794.\">Fixes</span> <a class=\"issue-link js-issue-link\" data-error-text=\"Failed to load title\" data-id=\"3334171970\" data-permission-text=\"Title is private\" data-url=\"https://github.com/mdn/content/issues/40794\" data-hovercard-type=\"issue\" data-hovercard-url=\"/mdn/content/issues/40794/hovercard\" href=\"https://github.com/mdn/content/issues/40794\">#40794</a></p>",
            "url": "https://github.com/mdn/content/pull/40795",
            "title": "Remove redundant indefinite articles from var/param/etc names",
            "date_modified": "2025-08-19T12:52:29.000Z",
            "date_published": "2025-08-19T12:50:01.000Z",
            "author": {
                "name": "lionel-rowe",
                "url": "https://github.com/lionel-rowe"
            }
        },
        {
            "content_html": "<img src=\"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/10711649?u=753be56b80f5a8d1f84ebff3db3999e829ceffe4&v=4\" width=\"64\" height=\"64\" alt=\"\"/><br/><h3 dir=\"auto\">Description</h3>\n<p dir=\"auto\">This PR improves the <strong>Callback function glossary page</strong> by clarifying the examples that illustrate synchronous vs asynchronous callbacks.</p>\n<ul dir=\"auto\">\n<li>Updated the synchronous example to show why <code class=\"notranslate\">console.log(value)</code> prints <code class=\"notranslate\">2</code> (because <code class=\"notranslate\">value = 2</code> has already run).</li>\n<li>Simplified explanatory text for beginners while keeping it technically accurate.</li>\n</ul>\n<h3 dir=\"auto\">Motivation</h3>\n<p dir=\"auto\">The previous example was incomplete and sometimes confusing for readers.<br>\nI’ve received feedback that when sharing the page, the example “didn’t work” for people who had not yet read other parts of the documentation, because the context was missing.<br>\nThese changes make the examples self-contained and explicit, so they work for first-time readers as well as those familiar with other MDN docs.</p>",
            "url": "https://github.com/mdn/content/pull/40792",
            "title": "Clarify example in Callback function",
            "date_modified": "2025-08-19T10:11:21.000Z",
            "date_published": "2025-08-19T10:10:59.000Z",
            "author": {
                "name": "alexcastrodev",
                "url": "https://github.com/alexcastrodev"
            }
        },
        {
            "content_html": "<img src=\"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/5368500?v=4\" width=\"64\" height=\"64\" alt=\"\"/><br/><p dir=\"auto\">This updates <code class=\"notranslate\">ShadowRoot.innerHTML</code> property to the pattern we're using to document the need for trusted types on injection sinks.</p>\n<p dir=\"auto\">This doc is virtually a copy of the <code class=\"notranslate\">Element.innerHTML</code>. The differences are because this is a shadow root.</p>\n<p dir=\"auto\">The one thing I omitted I think might be relevant was <a href=\"https://developer.mozilla.org/en-US/docs/Web/API/Element/innerHTML#shadow_dom_considerations\" rel=\"nofollow\">https://developer.mozilla.org/en-US/docs/Web/API/Element/innerHTML#shadow_dom_considerations</a> - I suspect it is true because the algorithms are virtually the same -  but I couldn't verify from the spec.</p>\n<p dir=\"auto\">Related docs work is being tracked in <a class=\"issue-link js-issue-link\" data-error-text=\"Failed to load title\" data-id=\"2770544982\" data-permission-text=\"Title is private\" data-url=\"https://github.com/mdn/content/issues/37518\" data-hovercard-type=\"issue\" data-hovercard-url=\"/mdn/content/issues/37518/hovercard?comment_id=2629763658&amp;comment_type=issue_comment\" href=\"https://github.com/mdn/content/issues/37518#issuecomment-2629763658\">#37518 (comment)</a></p>",
